Manage the key groups whose keys sign the URLs and cookies of the signed
behaviors (--access signed --key-group ID). A group holds several keys, so that a
new key is added before the old one is removed. The private key of a key
generated by the server is returned once: nexoctl saves it under its
configuration directory (keys/ALIAS/KEYID.pem), where "dist sign-url" finds it,
or in --key-out.

Usage:
  nexoctl dist keygroup [flags]
  nexoctl dist keygroup [command]

Available Commands:
  create      Create a key group with a first key pair
  key         Add and remove the keys of a key group
  list        List the key groups and their keys
  remove      Remove a key group no distribution uses

Flags:
  -h, --help   help for keygroup

Global Flags:
      --config-dir string   configuration directory (default $NEXOCTL_CONFIG_DIR or ~/.nexoctl)
      --debug               dump the HTTP requests and responses on stderr, with the secrets redacted
      --json                print JSON Lines (one object per line with a "status" member)
      --no-color            disable colors (also with the NO_COLOR environment variable)
  -q, --quiet               hide confirmations and progress (results and errors are still printed)

Use "nexoctl dist keygroup [command] --help" for more information about a command.
